cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data, please cite the release you used."
type: dataset
title: "Terramechanics Reference Data"
abstract: >-
  Versioned physical-test data with point-level provenance for simulation-to-reality gap analysis
  of terramechanics simulators, beginning with soil tests recovered from Apollo-era reports. Every
  number is traceable to its printed page, carries a reading bound and a status that says how it
  was checked, and is given in SI with the printed value kept.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24477009"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/uwsbel/terramechanics-reference-data"
authors:
  - family-names: Negrut
    given-names: Dan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1565-2784"
    affiliation: "Simulation-Based Engineering Laboratory, University of Wisconsin-Madison"
  - family-names: Serban
    given-names: Radu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4219-905X"
    affiliation: "Simulation-Based Engineering Laboratory, University of Wisconsin-Madison"
keywords:
  - terramechanics
  - granular media
  - lunar soil simulants
  - Apollo
  - load-penetration
  - direct shear
  - simulation-to-reality
  - validation data
